name 'iterating-with-ai-preassessment-q9_2025'

question 'Which of the following describes a pure function?'

wrong 'A function that changes a global variable every time it runs.'
right 'A function that produces the same output every time it is given the same input and has no "side effects."'
wrong 'A function that was written entirely by an AI without human help.'
wrong 'A function that only works with numbers and never with strings.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 7

Pure functions are predictable and safer because they don't modify anything outside of themselves (no side effects), making them easier to test and reuse.
MARKDOWN
